[{:db/id 17592186162110 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-75ff021f-12e0-504a-b1eb-e811b2e15c5c" "question-8cf1eb9f-850d-5920-b6a9-b29ec6415a62" "question-423b0b62-7d55-5176-ba2c-330867aaba9c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-75ff021f-12e0-504a-b1eb-e811b2e15c5c" :question/id #uuid "75ff021f-12e0-504a-b1eb-e811b2e15c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143300" :question/problem "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{36}∼N(4,{18}^{2})$ is a random sample of size $36$ from a normal population, calculate $P(|\\overset{―}{X}|<2.07).$\n\n*Hint: Value tables of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.03\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2358\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2327\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2296\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2676\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2643\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2611\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3015\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2981\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2946\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.03\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-2.0\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0217\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0212\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0207\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-1.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0274\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0268\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0262\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-1.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0344\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0336\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0329\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(4,\\frac{{18}^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & ∼N(4,9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(|\\overset{―}{X}|<2.07).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|\\overset{―}{X}|<2.07) & =P(-2.07<\\overset{―}{X}<2.07) \\\\  & =P(\\frac{-2.07-4}{\\sqrt{9}}<Z<\\frac{2.07-4}{\\sqrt{9}}) \\\\  & =P(-2.02<Z<-0.64) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.64)-Φ(-2.02)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.64) & =0.2611, \\\\ Φ(-2.02) & =0.0217.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|\\overset{―}{X}|<2.07) & =Φ(-0.64)-Φ(-2.02) \\\\  & =0.2611-0.0217 \\\\  & =0.2394.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-12fb0d15-7794-5d04-99a5-b1fe70075584"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12fb0d15-7794-5d04-99a5-b1fe70075584" :answer-field/id #uuid "12fb0d15-7794-5d04-99a5-b1fe70075584" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3aa5c52e-8e77-5a89-a2be-c5d48e02d707" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9db63bf-dd9b-5997-b12d-fcd3929e098a" "answer-ebc99d50-e93c-5e52-936e-cb1d51cb3239" "answer-3aa5c52e-8e77-5a89-a2be-c5d48e02d707" "answer-cd6ec6ff-8efb-5177-9119-05dcb8065b19" "answer-3d1645e2-c686-52f4-a67a-bc7ecd062596"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9db63bf-dd9b-5997-b12d-fcd3929e098a" :answer/id #uuid "d9db63bf-dd9b-5997-b12d-fcd3929e098a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2089" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebc99d50-e93c-5e52-936e-cb1d51cb3239" :answer/id #uuid "ebc99d50-e93c-5e52-936e-cb1d51cb3239" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2141" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3aa5c52e-8e77-5a89-a2be-c5d48e02d707" :answer/id #uuid "3aa5c52e-8e77-5a89-a2be-c5d48e02d707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2394" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd6ec6ff-8efb-5177-9119-05dcb8065b19" :answer/id #uuid "cd6ec6ff-8efb-5177-9119-05dcb8065b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2617" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d1645e2-c686-52f4-a67a-bc7ecd062596" :answer/id #uuid "3d1645e2-c686-52f4-a67a-bc7ecd062596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2671" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8cf1eb9f-850d-5920-b6a9-b29ec6415a62" :question/id #uuid "8cf1eb9f-850d-5920-b6a9-b29ec6415a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-143278" :question/problem "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{72}∼N(11,{12}^{2})$ is a random sample of size $72$ from a normal population, calculate $P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3).$\n\n*Hint: Value tables of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5793\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5832\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5871\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6179\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6217\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6255\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6554\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6591\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6628\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3594\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3557\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3520\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3974\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3936\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3897\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,-0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4364\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4325\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4286\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(11,\\frac{{12}^{2}}{72}) \\\\  & ∼N(11,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3) & =P(\\frac{10.75-11}{\\sqrt{2}}<Z<\\frac{11.3-11}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =P(-0.18<Z<0.21) \\\\  & =Φ(0.21)-Φ(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.21)=0.5832, \\\\ Φ(-0.18)=0.4286.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10.75<\\overset{―}{X}<11.3) & =Φ(0.21)-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5832-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1546.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-71923c9e-37c2-5e23-b268-605b55085395"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-71923c9e-37c2-5e23-b268-605b55085395" :answer-field/id #uuid "71923c9e-37c2-5e23-b268-605b55085395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8656e755-f09d-585f-963c-1417a0c76564" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8656e755-f09d-585f-963c-1417a0c76564" "answer-e1912ce9-3c8a-5844-be84-93a3bc2ad545" "answer-6f7321b6-5af0-51ed-bd62-8af990e9830a" "answer-fcbb04c0-4a0c-5bc7-821d-d45839a72b1d" "answer-f411090e-554c-590e-a751-4616cba263c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8656e755-f09d-585f-963c-1417a0c76564" :answer/id #uuid "8656e755-f09d-585f-963c-1417a0c76564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1546" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1912ce9-3c8a-5844-be84-93a3bc2ad545" :answer/id #uuid "e1912ce9-3c8a-5844-be84-93a3bc2ad545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1703" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f7321b6-5af0-51ed-bd62-8af990e9830a" :answer/id #uuid "6f7321b6-5af0-51ed-bd62-8af990e9830a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1965" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcbb04c0-4a0c-5bc7-821d-d45839a72b1d" :answer/id #uuid "fcbb04c0-4a0c-5bc7-821d-d45839a72b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2268" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f411090e-554c-590e-a751-4616cba263c4" :answer/id #uuid "f411090e-554c-590e-a751-4616cba263c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2281" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-423b0b62-7d55-5176-ba2c-330867aaba9c" :question/id #uuid "423b0b62-7d55-5176-ba2c-330867aaba9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143303" :question/problem "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}∼N(-3,{8}^{2})$ is a random sample of size $16$ from a normal population, calculate $P(|\\overset{―}{X}|>0.5).$\n\n*Hint: Value tables of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,1.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8925\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8944\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8962\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,1.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9099\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9115\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9131\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,1.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9251\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9265\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9279\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"25%\">$z$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,1.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9505\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9515\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9525\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,1.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9599\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9608\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9616\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\,1.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9678\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9686\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9693\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a normal population, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ has the distribution\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(-3,\\frac{{8}^{2}}{16}) \\\\  & ∼N(-3,4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're required to find $P(|\\overset{―}{X}|>0.5).$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|\\overset{―}{X}|>0.5) & =1-P(|\\overset{―}{X}|<0.5) \\\\  & =1-P(-0.5<\\overset{―}{X}<0.5) \\\\  & =1-P(\\frac{-0.5-(-3)}{\\sqrt{4}}<Z<\\frac{0.5-(-3)}{\\sqrt{4}}) \\\\  & =1-P(1.25<Z<1.75) \\\\  & =1-(Φ(1.75)-Φ(1.25)) \\\\  & =1+Φ(1.25)-Φ(1.75)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.25) & =0.8944, \\\\ Φ(1.75) & =0.9599.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|\\overset{―}{X}|>0.5) & =1+Φ(1.25)-Φ(1.75) \\\\  & =1+0.8944-0.9599 \\\\  & =0.9345.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c4f53ce6-98d9-5812-993e-85598a8a0278"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c4f53ce6-98d9-5812-993e-85598a8a0278" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f53ce6-98d9-5812-993e-85598a8a0278" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-211e8525-9c7c-5f08-90b9-8bafbce89824" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9aced102-4694-5dd6-9412-58caa8ddf4d9" "answer-c8148e07-be44-5483-8044-795aa374f125" "answer-211e8525-9c7c-5f08-90b9-8bafbce89824" "answer-70ccaa0a-2296-5e47-9485-665082d89a91" "answer-69064a58-7535-5a5d-b74e-eda826922abc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aced102-4694-5dd6-9412-58caa8ddf4d9" :answer/id #uuid "9aced102-4694-5dd6-9412-58caa8ddf4d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8437" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8148e07-be44-5483-8044-795aa374f125" :answer/id #uuid "c8148e07-be44-5483-8044-795aa374f125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8807" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-211e8525-9c7c-5f08-90b9-8bafbce89824" :answer/id #uuid "211e8525-9c7c-5f08-90b9-8bafbce89824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9345" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70ccaa0a-2296-5e47-9485-665082d89a91" :answer/id #uuid "70ccaa0a-2296-5e47-9485-665082d89a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9420" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69064a58-7535-5a5d-b74e-eda826922abc" :answer/id #uuid "69064a58-7535-5a5d-b74e-eda826922abc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/v